    "own_line": true,
    "norm": "Tests that {@link AccountingChronology#dateYearDay(int, int)} rejects a day-of-year that exceeds the length of the given accounting year. <p>The chronology under test ends on SUNDAY nearest end of AUGUST, divides the year into thirteen 4-week months, and places the leap-week in month 13. A standard (non-leap) accounting year contains exactly 364 days, so day 366 is always invalid for a non-leap year such as 2001."
